{"title":"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Sal_Khan\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Sal Khan</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The members of a distinguished committee were choosing a president, and each member gave one vote to one of the 27 candidates.  For each candidate, the exact percentage of votes the candidate got was smaller by at least 1 than the number of votes for that candidate.  What was the smallest possible number of members of the committee?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/f/85ffd98b4eaea58a8db38fd0047e3a1d7c5661a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of votes candidate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> received, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/5/9c5fc213231e9806273011520c9ad832dcdd2d84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=v_1+\\cdots+v_{27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"136\" height=\"13\" /> be the total number of votes cast. Our goal is to determine the smallest possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>Candidate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> got <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/e/78e4165796babefd4b1b8082086be4227fef9742.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{v_i}s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"16\" height=\"33\" /> of the votes, hence the percentage of votes they received is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/5/d157420d186d39dcda2d6aff5317a0fcb2974c7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{100v_i}s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"44\" height=\"37\" />. The condition in the problem statement says that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/c/e5c1a59def7fc0528a4ea576ef6b974add78db32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\forall i: \\frac{100v_i}s + 1 \\leq v_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"146\" height=\"37\" />.  (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/6/536ba5a392431e74fec5a8db2257504c85fcc206.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\forall$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"10\" height=\"13\" /> means \"for all\", so this means \"For all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/f/78f26ae9c19ccb4453ae219618ce6ee572ec0aad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{100v_i}s + 1 \\leq v_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"117\" height=\"38\" /> is true\")\n</p><p>Obviously, if some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/f/85ffd98b4eaea58a8db38fd0047e3a1d7c5661a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the condition would be false. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/6/fd67065bf5eafbbe6f345b6d7478abf9975df90b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\forall i: v_i\\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"15\" />. We can then rewrite the above inequality as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/f/7cf40436d11fb36dbf0a684eedcc2c20a375e5ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\forall i: s\\geq\\frac{100v_i}{v_i-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"112\" height=\"40\" />. \n</p><p>If for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/6/65639cf2759d14c2a176983323d7c1b8a45bf07b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_i=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />, then from the inequality we just derived we would have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/a/dfa4660f4e5a3ea34ce25860692ce3530226d963.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s\\geq 200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>If for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/7/807efb6e87e534ccc77ccfe0f3c3e577d97f2d5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_i=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/7/0971d988783603affc314614d38cb7db890637b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s\\geq 150$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>And if for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdb0b958c29558ca21821e52620b22cb460a67b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_i=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/0/fa01f681e6042c3563ccf8550ef7638172322faa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s\\geq \\frac{400}3 = 133\\frac13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"127\" height=\"37\" />, and hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/d/7ed98694fe8b0aa08b6c3649b57b1e94816da0d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s\\geq 134$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Is it possible to have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/d/1bd2c69a8429a4851b7b0a735182ba1355388de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s&lt;134$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />? We just proved that to have such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/f/85ffd98b4eaea58a8db38fd0047e3a1d7c5661a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> have to be at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. But then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/6/126305e8aa92a37ad65d65e662de91cc05978fe8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=v_1+\\cdots+v_{27}\\geq 27\\cdot 5 = 135$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"253\" height=\"15\" />, which is a contradiction. Hence the smallest possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/9/489263c8336e32dbda8c2160060f5aacb822c9e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$134$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Now consider a situation where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/a/bda00d9a38a0c6bd9aac2512c6d065581882d43c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> candidates got <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> votes each, and one candidate got <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> votes. In this situation, the total number of votes is exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/9/489263c8336e32dbda8c2160060f5aacb822c9e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$134$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />, and for each candidate the above inequality is satisfied. Hence the minimum number of committee members is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/f/95f146fdd993a8467e4f0ca2b83588ebc30f2f48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=\\boxed{134}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Note: Each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/a/bda00d9a38a0c6bd9aac2512c6d065581882d43c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> candidates received <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/e/6ae1654c0586f98fa21f2a5d12c806af4c1dd51a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\simeq 3.63\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" /> votes, and the last candidate received <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/e/41e5e626defa722b90fbaa024d471a684213ee6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\simeq 2.985\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> votes.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let there be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> members of the committee.\nSuppose candidate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> gets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> votes.\nThen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> as a percentage out of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/340c8e64a3085c5443b4ba4df8281342fa208830.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100\\frac{a_n}{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"48\" height=\"33\" />. Setting up the inequality \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/e/5bee3d362e079ee1e804fa20733ca94f676f1644.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n \\geq 1 + 100\\frac{a_n}{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"122\" height=\"33\" /> and simplifying,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/9/3c9c5706c3374ea479a1fe75e6af84b1c6153cea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n \\geq \\lceil(\\frac{N}{N - 100})\\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"140\" height=\"38\" /> (the ceiling function is there because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> is an integer.\nNote that if we set all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/6/476ac990cc577bee0b43bcf78b4b6541c6e2ea71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lceil(\\frac{N}{N - 100})\\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"102\" height=\"41\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/f/96fed344d649873b4fd65ae39e4eedcf29bf048b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N \\geq 27\\lceil(\\frac{N}{N - 100})\\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"161\" height=\"41\" />. Starting from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/b/94bb6fb7a3ff722532798b45607025254679e7b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$101$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, try greater values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> to find which value is large enough. It helps to try <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> with multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> for ease of computation.Then when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/7/dc73035417d52d7ab8199446935fae3e73661c35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" />, the RHS equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/c/b1cabd694ac73746578171e5d1954daf9e9dc9bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27(5)=135$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" />, which is pretty close. As soon as the ceiling part equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, RHS equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/7/f97967aac029f4963153efdfee7850f8cfadc2e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$108\\le N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"17\" />. Solving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b9118370e2a73b02b58406b4cd969e4bfc299c40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{N}{N - 100}\\leq4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"105\" height=\"41\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a7465be7a20e7f8a9be1f6d211ef582dcee540.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 134$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"68\" height=\"13\" /> as the least such number that satisfies this inequality. Now we must show that we can find suitable <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />. We can let 26 of them equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and one of them equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or 26 equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and one equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/5/a35b324d82d51d234c1904e6d03abf94747e0801.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = \\boxed{134}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"81\" height=\"25\" /> is the answer.\n- whatRthose\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be the total number of people in the committee, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of votes candidate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> gets where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/5/605881926f1b38a430af5d4173f3cdd9df74d94a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq i \\leq 27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />.  The problem tells us that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/5/bd5e58fdb0f3e9c3398f0826d30a40a694572e6e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{100a_i}{n} \\leq a_i - 1 \\implies 100a_i \\leq na_i - n \\implies a_i \\geq \\frac{n}{n-100}.\\]\" width=\"447\" height=\"37\" />Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/b/b4bb3e345430fdb26baf8449eec4cdaa1096e74c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum^{27}_{i=1} a_i = n \\geq \\sum^{27}_{i=1} \\frac{n}{n-100} = \\frac{27n}{n-100},\\]\" width=\"288\" height=\"50\" />and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/d/7ad381973e6f7db579cc7bbf86a3da6a321478ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(n-127) \\geq 0 \\implies n \\geq 127$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"233\" height=\"20\" />.  Trying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/6/d1636afc46bea8ea464afe6c1587295b605d84e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 127$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/b/d6bb60ad6b1d2bbf1bc5eccf4a5aa7f696d4c0db.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_i \\geq \\frac{127}{27} \\approx 4.7 \\implies a_i \\geq 5 \\implies \\sum^{27}_{a_i} a_i \\geq 5 \\cdot 27 = 135 \\geq 127,\\]\" width=\"478\" height=\"52\" />a contradiction.  Bashing out a few more, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/3/f334563fa529f048a8ffde4e0ce7e880923d0372.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{n = 134}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"76\" height=\"25\" /> works perfectly fine.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Sal_Khan\">Video Solution by Sal Khan</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Sal Khan\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KD46pC_KFWk&amp;list=PLSQl0a2vh4HCtW1EiNlfW_YoNAA38D0l4&amp;index=10\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KD46pC_KFWk&amp;list=PLSQl0a2vh4HCtW1EiNlfW_YoNAA38D0l4&amp;index=10</a>\n- AMBRIGGS\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II\" title=\"2003 AIME II\">2003 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2003 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2003\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2003 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017201249\nCache expiry: 86400\nR